WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.350
The new school term began and
we became second-year students.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.290
Taking the places of the
Lady Roses who graduated,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.150
Sachiko-sama has become the Rosa Chinensis,

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.190
Rei-sama the Rosa Foetida,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.690
and Shimako-san the Rosa Gigantea.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.760
Next, we have the Maria Festival
being held in the middle of May.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.640
The priest will be bringing the medallions...

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.200
...to be presented to the
first-year students on that day,

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.200
so we are to meet him in
the morning to receive them.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.040
That task will fall to the two boutons.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.270
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:52.640
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.270
And Rosa Gigantea,

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.410
with regards to the roses to
be pinned to our chests...

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.930
S-Shimako-san?

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:14.500
Shimako-san.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.030
Oh, yes?

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.650
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:36.420
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.220
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.100
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.560
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.900
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:56.440
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:09.490
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:18.530
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:25.440
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:32.980
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:40.640
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:48.130
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:55.600
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:03.750
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:11.150
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:18.080
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:26.090
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.910
Cherry Blossoms

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.150
Shimako-san is acting strange.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.290
What?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:32.000
She seems sort of listless,
like she has no energy...

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.740
And whenever she has some time,

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.470
she apparently goes behind
the auditorium alone...

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.030
...to look at the cherry blossoms.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.440
Cherry blossoms, huh?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:42.870
I see.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:43.940
What is it?

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.710
The cherry blossoms played a part...

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.770
...in bringing Shimako-san
and Sei-sama together, so...

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.140
They did?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.550
I hear it was under the cherry tree that
Sei-sama gave her the rosary, too.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.690
With Sei-sama gone now, I want
to be there for Shimako-san, but...

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.030
Year 2, Pine Class

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.070
Year 2, Pine Class
Come to think of it, this will be the first
time you and I are in the same class.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.300
Come to think of it, this will be the first
time you and I are in the same class.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.890
Yes, finally, after 13 years,
all the way from kindergarten.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:16.470
I wonder if Shimako-san is still allowing
herself to be lost in her memories.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.740
Or could she have something
else troubling her?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.910
Well, let's just wait and see until
the cherry blossoms scatter.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.360
If Shimako-san still isn't back
to her old self at that point,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.120
we'll go talk to Rei-chan
and Sachiko-sama about it.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.450
My Onee-sama?

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:33.860
Is something wrong with that?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:35.560
No...

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.970
During spring vacation,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:41.260
I was hoping that something fun would happen,

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:42.700
but nothing happened.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.840
On top of that, with the new school term,

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.860
we don't get to spend much time together, so...

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.050
I'll take that sorrowful expression, thank you!

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.110
Tsutako-san!

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.380
And Mami-san!

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:55.620
The caption will be,

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.050
"The Melancholy of the
Rosa Chinensis en bouton."

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.150
So, what happened between
you and Sachiko-sama?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.220
So? What happened?!

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:07.160
Oh, I can't believe I'm in the
same class with them, too!

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:22.480
I am different from those girls.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.810
I knew that, even before I entered this school.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.480
That day, if only it hadn't snowed...

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.030
These cherry blossoms will be
past their prime after today...

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.630
It would have been a shame
to enjoy them all by myself,

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.470
so it's perfect that someone
else has come to see them.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.530
Is it because the cherry
blossoms are so beautiful...

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.190
...that you have forgotten?

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.160
What?

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.200
How to speak.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.640
I just remembered how...

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:01.640
G-Good day.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.340
Good day.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:04.910
I'm so glad.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:08.120
I was worried that we would
not have a chance to speak,

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.880
even though you had joined me here.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.660
Um, do you come here every day?

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.190
Yes, pretty much, ever since the
cherry blossoms started to bloom.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.160
Drawn out here by this tree...

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.560
There are many other beautiful cherry trees,

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.260
but I don't feel specially drawn
to them as I am to this tree.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.970
I wonder why that is...

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:43.250
Standing alone among gingko trees...

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:47.150
Because it's all by itself, and yet,
it can blossom so beautifully...

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:58.630
Yes, it really is exactly as you say.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.070
I should go now.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.500
Um, in your hair, too.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.340
Thank you.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.120
Let's meet again.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:00.790
Yes.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.200
Looking up at cherry blossoms
and becoming lost in thought...

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:15.770
That's not exactly unusual
behavior for a teenage girl.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:19.980
In truth, Shimako-san must want to see you,
Rosa Gigantea.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.280
But she is resisting the urge...

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.850
Well, I should hope so.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:30.020
It's still only been a month since I graduated.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.730
The high school and college buildings...

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.200
...are a stone's throw away from each other.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.760
Being so close and yet not really, it must be...

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:40.790
So? Are those the only troubles
you wanted to discuss?

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:41.960
What?

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.570
Isn't there something going on with you, too?

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:49.870
During the cherry blossom season,
Sachiko can get irate or listless, so...

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.810
But it's kind of like hay fever, okay?

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.080
As always, you know everything,
don't you, Rosa Gigantea?

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.080
Well then, I have a lecture to go to.

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.990
And would you stop calling me Rosa Gigantea?

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.760
After all, Shimako's the Rosa Gigantea now.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.990
Then... Sei-sama?

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.390
I'm not too keen about that, either.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:14.290
What would you like to be called?

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.930
Sei-san. Or possibly Sato-san.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.800
Personally speaking, I'm on a
"Sato-san" kick right now, by the way.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.040
See you.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.130
Where were you?

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.360
I am very sorry!

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.660
Please do not respond in a way
that does not answer my question.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:50.600
We were to discuss the Maria
Festival after school today.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.070
You cannot tell me that you
had forgotten about that.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.370
N-No...

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.380
And after the Maria Festival,

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.850
there's the Yamayuri Council Welcoming
Ceremony for the first-year students.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.310
You had not forgotten that too, I hope.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:02.980
Of course not.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:05.210
So, where were you?

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.520
Um, I was meeting a friend...

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.090
...whom I had parted with when
the school year ended.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.960
And thus, you did not make
it to our meeting on time.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:23.770
Who's that?

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.470
Toko-chan.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.840
But Sachiko Onee-sama,
I find myself so amused...

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.840
...by this person.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.910
"Sachiko Onee-sama"?

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.390
Toko-chan, stop calling me that.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.490
But that's what I've always called you.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.200
At the very least, while we are at school,

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.140
call me "Sachiko-sama" or " Rosa Chinensis."

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.370
Mixing public and private matters is not good.

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.880
Let me introduce you, Yumi.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.880
This is Matsudaira Toko-chan.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.110
She's a new student.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:11.870
She dropped by, because she
wanted to see the Rose Mansion.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:13.680
Nice to meet you.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:16.660
I'm a relative of Sachiko Onee-sama's.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.790
I had heard you were a distant relation.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.120
But a relative, nonetheless.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.660
So, Onee-sama, about today's discussion...

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.500
It's been canceled.

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:34.230
What?

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.800
Because Rei was unable to attend.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:42.610
Then what did I get relentlessly
reproached about my tardiness for?

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.240
Sachiko Onee-sama,

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:47.380
this place is so comfortable.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.120
I've fallen in love with it.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.920
Maybe I'll come visit again.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.250
Don't overdo it, now.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.130
Yumi-san, you'd better watch out.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.330
If you don't pay attention,
you're going to lose your Onee-sama to her.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.300
But...

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.740
I'm my Onee-sama's petite soeur...

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:18.380
Noriko-san.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.760
Um...

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.300
I'm Toko, I'm in your class.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.800
You still don't remember my name?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.230
I'm sorry about that.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.330
I was just at the Rose Mansion.

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:38.770
The Rose Mansion?

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.510
It's sort of like the office of the student council.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:43.140
I went because the Lady Roses were there.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.570
Lady Roses?

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.480
Yes, there was a meeting
about the Maria Festival.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:48.970
The Maria Festival?

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:53.350
Noriko-san, you really don't know
anything about Lillian, do you?

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.390
The Maria Festival is a festival
that is unique to Lillian.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.520
I see.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.600
It's called a festival,

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.860
but we don't set up shops
and there are no presentations...

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:06.160
...like for the school festival.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.970
We adorn all the Maria-sama statues
here at the academy with flowers,

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.130
and in place of classes, we have mass.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.310
Also, in your first-year in high school,

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.380
there's something to look
forward to after the mass.

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:21.210
Our dear sisters in the student council
hold a welcoming ceremony for us.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.120
Oh, look.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.180
Those are the Lady Roses.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:30.610
Starting from the front,

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.990
Rosa Chinensis, Rosa Foetida,

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:37.120
and Rosa Gigantea.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.700
During the Maria Festival,

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:45.500
the Lady Roses will welcome
us as their new little sisters.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:48.260
It's her...

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.180
It's her!

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:24.240
Shimako-san... seems happy?

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.740
Shimako has been behaving strangely.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.510
I am aware of that.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.620
When the Rosa Gig...
I mean, when Sei-sama left,

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.850
I imagined that she would become listless.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:38.190
A kind of reactionary thing, if you will.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:39.490
No matter how they looked,

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:43.330
those two were still emotionally
dependent on each other.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:47.890
For our part, we were planning on
taking advantage of that fact.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.390
Taking advantage?

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:54.230
Wouldn't you like to see Shimako open up?

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.340
What?

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:59.110
Up until now, Sei-sama had posted
herself in front of the door,

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:00.510
so it was difficult, but now...

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:01.580
I see...

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:06.690
But lately, Shimako seems oddly happy somehow.

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:08.090
You're right.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:10.520
Could it be that you have the door open,

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.690
so we'll know immediately
when Shimako-san comes?

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:16.520
Right. When Shimako arrives,
we suspend this discussion.

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.230
Do you two know Shimako's story?

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:46.690
Whenever I have time, I travel to
temples to admire Buddhist statues,

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:50.500
and yet, to find myself ending up
enrolled at a Catholic school...

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:55.170
The day before the exam for
my first choice high school,

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.900
I was in Kyoto...

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:00.270
...to see the Kannon statue
that is put on exhibition...

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:02.140
...only once every 20 years.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.740
But on my way home,

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.740
the bullet train service was
suspended due to heavy snow...

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:13.080
...and I ended up enrolling at Lillian,
which I had tested for...

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.480
...out of respect for my great aunt.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.230
I had not expected such a
young person to come here.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:40.180
Um, is the Miroku statue that you
have here really the work of Yuukai?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.070
That is how it has been passed down to us.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:44.880
But you are...

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.380
...neither a scholar nor an appraiser,

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:53.090
so perhaps you need only view it
without any worldly thoughts?

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.520
Yes, Sir.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.990
Ah, here we are.

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.660
I have brought the Miroku statue.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.520
This is my daughter, Shimako.

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.060
I have some business to attend to now,

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.090
so I will leave you two young people to it.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.960
Why?

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:42.440
Why is she here?

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:45.400
Would you like to see it?

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:53.540
It's beautiful!

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:57.450
I feel as though my spirit is purified!

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:02.120
The Miroku Buddha by Yuukai...

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.960
...is not an object connected
with Shoguji Temple.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.460
Rather, it's been passed down in our
family from generation to generation.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:13.340
We rarely show it to people,

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:18.180
but it seems an acquaintance of my
father's prevailed upon him to show it.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:21.080
Because there was a lady who
loved Buddhist statues...

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.590
I never imagined that it would be you.

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:52.800
I'm so sorry.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:57.650
We only get one bus every
hour on non-business days.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.450
N-Not at all...

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:19.730
Don't move.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:30.410
Shoguji Temple

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.130
So, no questions?

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:51.170
What?

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:55.910
About how I am the daughter
of a temple household,

00:21:56.380 --> 00:22:00.210
and yet, attend Lillian Girls' Academy...

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:02.880
And about how that is contradictory...

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:29.760
Shimako-san and Noriko-san!
Oh, what will happen to the two of them?!

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:31.710
What will happen?! What will happen?!

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:33.610
